(1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-2) & =0 \\\\ 4-\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-5)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =25-32 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426471 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426466 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426471 1069 "q-76362" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426471 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426471 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426471 1072 #uuid "95fd78c2-6907-5df8-b9fe-1452968ce01b" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426471 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(\\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426472 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426465 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426472 1069 "q-9339" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426472 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426472 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426472 1072 #uuid "aaa6413c-ed34-5909-9e88-242b0b85efde" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426472 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426473 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426469 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426473 1069 "q-36766" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426473 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426473 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426473 1072 #uuid "dca9fe6d-d02a-5d80-b4d4-5f9b25f0fbc8" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426473 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3+\\lambda ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534581 17592186045417 true] [17592186426474 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426468 13194139534581 17592186045417 tr